Change: Take the bundled market app from its own repository

The market app existed twice: as its own repository (BWTECH-github/market) and
as the copy under apps-external/market that ships in the release package. The
two had drifted apart. Every fix had to be applied by hand in both places; the
bundled copy still called itself "ownCloud" in its summary and description,
linked to the wrong repository, and shipped a vendor/ directory holding only a
Composer development plugin (bamarni/composer-bin-plugin) that nothing loads.

The repository is now the only source. build/sync-market.sh copies a given
commit of it into apps-external/market - every versioned file except .github/,
.gitignore and tests/ - and records the commit in build/market.ref. The push
check (job market-copy in .github/workflows/lint-and-codestyle.yml) compares the committed
copy with the recorded commit on every push to main and fails if the copy was
edited directly.

The PHP code of both copies was already identical once comments are ignored,
and so was the JavaScript bundle; the app version stays 0.10.10, so no upgrade
is triggered on existing instances.
